  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A calendar can display both possible garden sessions and volunteers’ available times.\", \"decision\": \"How should volunteers find a working session they can attend?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteers add garden sessions directly to the calendar and invite others with matching available times. Small groups can form without waiting for a complete schedule.\nThe coordinator places possible garden sessions on the calendar before volunteers choose available times. A proposed schedule gives volunteers a common starting point.\nVolunteers mark available times before the coordinator places garden sessions on the calendar. Sessions follow overlapping availability."
    }
  ],
